# fixedbugs, defect 570, lane b18-guard, 2026-10-10 (panel 205's R1).
#
# SYMPTOM: through a header writing `#pragma clang diagnostic ignored
# "-Wincompatible-function-pointer-types"`, a callback declared
# `(function(x: i64) -> i64)` against `void (*)(void)` built and ran it.
#
# CAUSE: clang makes the warning an error by default, and the header's
# pragma turned it off at the probe.
#
# FIX: after the groups' includes, and again at the probe region, every
# warning a check of a binding rests on is raised again
# (`emit/checks_raised.hero`), the build's `-Werror` words and clang's three
# default errors, so the message is the one a plain header gets.

extern "fixedbugs-570-a-callback-of-another-type-is-refused-through-the-pragma.h"
    function run_cb(f: (function(x: i64) -> i64)) -> i32  #~ ffi_callback_type

function cb(x: i64) -> i64
    return x

function main()
    print(run_cb(cb))
